<title>UK: Capita upbeat after buoyant sales in Q1.</title>
<headline>Capita upbeat after buoyant sales in Q1.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Business services group Capita Group Plc said on Tuesday that at the end of the first quarter sales were &quot;very substantially ahead&quot; of the same period in 1996.</p>
<p>Rod Aldridge, chairman and chief executive of Capita, told the firm's annual meeting that sales activity continues to be buoyant and that he was positive about the group's performance for the year as a whole.</p>
<p>Capita made pretax profit of 12.3 million stg in 1996.</p>
<p>By 0949 GMT, shares in the company had risen 50p to stand at 685p.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
